### Investigation summary (root cause)

| Question | Finding |
| :--- | :--- |
| What exactly is broken? | `views.activatePanel` calls `desktopApi.setActivePanel(panel)`, which does not exist in the dockview api → `TypeError`. |
| When is it reached? | Only from `ui.showApp`'s de-duplication branch (`existingApp` by `key`, or `existingPanel` by `component`+`initialParams`) — i.e. when a panel is *focused* rather than created. |
| Why only Task Manager panels with a `board`? | `tasks` is the only `multiInstance` app whose instance identity is param-derived (`desktopKey`/`desktopTabId` → `tasks-<board>`). With a board, `key === tabId === tasks-<board>` is stable across store / dockview panel / saved layout, so re-opening that board always lands on the de-dup branch and `getPanel(id)` resolves to a live panel → the broken line executes. Without a board, `desktopTabId` returns `undefined` (generated id) and the launcher passes `newInstance: true` (skips de-dup), so the path is not taken. |
| Fix | Activate the panel through dockview's own api (`panel.api.setActive()`), with a version-tolerant fallback. No layout/state changes. |

